// induction with (2i - 1), n-th odd number
theorem: for all n in N, sum from i=1 to n of (2i - 1) = n^2
proof
we proceed by induction on n.
base case n = 0: the empty sum is 0 = 0^2.
inductive step: assume sum from i=1 to k of (2i - 1) = k^2.
the (k+1)st odd number is 2(k+1) - 1 = 2k + 1, so the sum up to k+1 is k^2 + 2k + 1 = (k + 1)^2.
qed
